  "notes": "The article writes the analyzed composition as Al0.98(1)Si0.92(1)O3OH1.39(5). This is condensed hydroxyl notation for Al0.98Si0.92H1.39O4 (three O plus one O bearing 1.39 H), consistent with the official CIF analytical formula; it is not O4.39. The deposited 2018 X-ray structure fixes Al and Si occupancies to unity because refined and fixed-occupancy models were indistinguishable, and it contains no H atom site. The ideal fully occupied structural model therefore has Al4Si4H4O16 cell contents and is a diffraction model for the analyzed Al3.92Si3.68H5.56O16 composition, not an assertion that the measured vacancies or excess hydrogen were crystallographically resolved. The H coordinate is the powder-XRD position from Schmidt et al. (1998) explicitly used in the 2018 paper's Figure 1. The structural ambient volume, 214.431(13) A^3, differs from fitted V0 because the authors excluded the in-house ambient point from the synchrotron EOS regression.",
